    "title": "'Ghost hunt' comes to Topeka Cemetery on Saturday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Amy Acevedo ,\n37 minutes ago\nTOPEKA ( KSNT ) – Paranormal enthusiasts are going on a ‘ghost hunt’ at the Topeka Cemetery this weekend.\nGhost Light Paranormal of Topeka hopes guest will be able to “commune with the spirits” at the historic cemetery, while also learning about the many historical figures who are laid to rest there.\n“You’ve got some really amazing historians that know every inch of this cemetery that are going to be here, that are going to be able to tell us who was here, why they were here, why they’re important to Topeka and northeast Kansas,” Scott Price said, the founder of Ghost Light Paranormal.\nGhost Light Paranormal will bring its own equipment to ‘hunt’ for spirits, while also giving guests the opportunity to test it out for themselves.\n“You just don’t go to the hardware store and just look for things you use to communicate with spirits,” Price said. “A lot of the equipment we use is used for other purposes, like finding electromagnetic field leaks or radio frequencies.”\nThe event starts at 6 p.m. and runs through 11 p.m. All ticket proceeds will go toward the Historic Topeka Cemetery. They can be purchased on Ghost Light Paranormal’s Facebook page or at the gate.\nFor more Kansas news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news in northeast Kansas by downloading our mobile app and by signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track Weather app by clicking here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSNT 27 News.",
